#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124159 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "0a8f5141-941d-5059-9d9f-bf9e5b09096f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3127" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac {\\partial^2 f }{\\partial x\\partial y}$ given that $\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial y} =  \\dfrac {2y} {x + y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\dfrac {\\partial^2 f }{\\partial x\\partial y},$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2y}{x+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({(x+{y}^{2})}^{-1}) \\\\  & =-2y(x+{y}^{2})^{-2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124160 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "e16f6686-dffb-554e-a50a-8760e818439f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3129" :question/problem "Find $f_{xy}(x,y)+f_{yx}(x,y)$ given that  $f_x(x,y)=y\\cos(xy)$ and $f_y(x,y)=x\\cos(xy).$" :question/worked-solution "To find $f_{xy}(x,y),$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $f_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+y(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSimilarly, to find $f_{yx}(x,y),$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $f_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+x(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124161 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "a41bfb06-4372-5124-b910-4b35f19d148b" :question/math-academy-id "e-3130" :question/problem "Evaluate $g_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,2,3)$ if $g_x(x,y,z) = 2x y z +  y^3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $g_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating $g_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xyz+{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =2xz+3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $g_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating $g_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xz+3{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xyz}(1,2,3) & =2(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cfc9712-8c3b-5fa3-a33b-11b626f9ef09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321681} {:answer/id #uuid "99bfc043-8f68-508b-91ad-e548faaebfec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321682} {:answer/id #uuid "7b71161f-383c-5ecd-991f-f62df20a4569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321683} {:answer/id #uuid "ffeae17a-a81a-5e99-902d-4a1a75c6a96a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321684} {:answer/id #uuid "96636a31-e8aa-5e12-aed3-96daaa4aab70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b71161f-383c-5ecd-991f-f62df20a4569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321683} :answer-field/id #uuid "925e59f4-5c72-5cc1-997b-49bfd382f6c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37621ae1-7e64-5bc8-ad38-b498496d3d59" :question/math-academy-id "q-132764" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{2{x}^{2}+y}{{y}^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\frac{2{x}^{2}+y}{{y}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}+y) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}(4x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "790f0d5e-8884-5699-b850-717ffa2c3084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{y}}{(x+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321688} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb699c5-e393-5d38-8e4f-e34e1ab1cf28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{y}}{(x-y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321689} {:answer/id #uuid "99162c7a-690f-5d4a-95f9-e14612860c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{y}(x+y-1)}{(x+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321690} {:answer/id #uuid "e195f742-5cb1-53e7-9517-d1d1fbc83d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{y}}{(x+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321691} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb9f87d-c3b7-54d6-b3bd-5738b569a7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{(x+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e195f742-5cb1-53e7-9517-d1d1fbc83d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{y}}{(x+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321691} :answer-field/id #uuid "b23b0b0d-d232-5e2e-a5aa-003d9bed1ee4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2182bdc-83a4-50d6-86d3-87930fd17c32" :question/math-academy-id "q-132800" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{{e}^{y}}{x+y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{e}^{y}}{x+y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{y}}{(x+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d90a2fe-3a0e-567d-877f-bb42f34fca9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321695} {:answer/id #uuid "70000d0e-009f-58bc-bac3-c98a526d4055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321696} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc6499a-fd7a-5c94-ab9b-86887fb1a414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321697} {:answer/id #uuid "74e8fe9e-962c-5c86-9e49-368d3d928e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2xy}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321698} {:answer/id #uuid "d348807a-79ec-5100-8ae8-f8e91cc7a68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d90a2fe-3a0e-567d-877f-bb42f34fca9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321695} :answer-field/id #uuid "47854b94-911d-52f2-b21d-a72b251bac35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ded636a1-bfab-5a77-9994-1e43081f6a8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132875" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f976fb1a-8e05-5b3b-afe8-98786eb10a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321702} {:answer/id #uuid "4a6e0624-85ff-5862-81e3-3518814477e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321703} {:answer/id #uuid "05ae4dab-6217-5d45-9daa-124b3ebe7f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321704} {:answer/id #uuid "3a843fb8-ed5b-522b-ac6b-b89192d4aba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321705} {:answer/id #uuid "c58704fe-6aee-5ea6-b85e-e0dd2e1a3a6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f976fb1a-8e05-5b3b-afe8-98786eb10a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321702} :answer-field/id #uuid "096ebacf-d3a4-57e5-9588-292760252d78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7cc4a771-b441-5088-905e-971d433b9763" :question/math-academy-id "q-132891" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)\\cdot {g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(0,1)$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=2{e}^{2x-y}$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=-{e}^{2x-y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{e}^{2x-y}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{2x-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{e}^{2x-y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(0,1) & =4{e}^{2(0)-1}=4{e}^{-1} \\\\ {g}_{yy}(0,1) & ={e}^{2(0)-1}={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xx}(0,1)\\cdot {g}_{yy}(0,1)=4{e}^{-1}\\cdot {e}^{-1}=4{e}^{-2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91bd31df-5309-558f-a926-82da940f21b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321709} {:answer/id #uuid "c8fce30e-4a9a-5f75-8bf2-f72339df3efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321710} {:answer/id #uuid "225cef05-e4f3-5d19-8ccd-8d3fdc55eb09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321711} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf0dc0b-4e2a-514b-8843-40f32a289210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321712} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f7d2ab-d3b3-5f1a-866d-e571022d6c0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91bd31df-5309-558f-a926-82da940f21b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321709} :answer-field/id #uuid "13de9159-5c67-5f9d-a5c4-abc83e011769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e4c13f2-d7be-519c-b88f-355c27cc03a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-132897" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)+{g}_{yx}(x,y)$ at $(-1,2)$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x+2y}$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{2}{x+2y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{x+2y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(x+2y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2}{x+2y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(x+2y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xy}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yx}(x,y)$ at $(-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(-1,2) & =-\\frac{2}{((-1)+2(2))^{2}}=-\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ {g}_{yx}(-1,2) & =-\\frac{2}{((-1)+2(2))^{2}}=-\\frac{2}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xy}(-1,2)+{g}_{yx}(-1,2)=-\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321714 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44d51cea-5855-59b3-8e90-e9b235ab1fba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321716} {:answer/id #uuid "93687c3f-4873-5a2e-bd80-c36784b98df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321717} {:answer/id #uuid "7720eac2-7227-5274-b30e-099a6955fafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321718} {:answer/id #uuid "0561a2a8-2fcc-5572-96ff-df92d77932e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321719} {:answer/id #uuid "68964bce-db0f-53b4-a514-d148f52dabff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7720eac2-7227-5274-b30e-099a6955fafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321718} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dd68d30-096e-5201-8a7e-a7cef951571b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a0c6f830-201a-5907-abfd-ac0c89aa4495" :question/math-academy-id "q-132940" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(-5,2,3)$ for $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+z).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+z)) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+z)) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y+z} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{y+z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{2x}{y+z}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{1}{y+z}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{(y+z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{(y+z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(-5,2,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(-5,2,3) & =-\\frac{2(-5)}{(2+3)^{2}}=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7461a1c5-a4a9-58d3-8fcc-314f7414a508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321723} {:answer/id #uuid "af4a9766-e350-5511-822f-4f0f6c812d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321724} {:answer/id #uuid "a365acee-007d-5f2e-9fcf-19854a1794da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321725} {:answer/id #uuid "9c71b7fc-f26d-5a5a-9647-6482d9d39b4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321726} {:answer/id #uuid "8c0550b4-7dac-592a-b59a-94f534d4d874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c71b7fc-f26d-5a5a-9647-6482d9d39b4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321726} :answer-field/id #uuid "742611f3-c4c7-542b-9c90-2a48a56ed775" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee9df1f5-cb1d-59c5-8894-54201c221d7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132961" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{xxz}(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi )$ for $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡xyz) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\cdot yz \\\\  & =yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot (-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xx}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xx}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\cdot (2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)+xy{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}z(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)+xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ) & =-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi )+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfedf5a1-9300-5e95-aff5-d40a62141369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122207} {:answer/id #uuid "18fe4be6-f80a-5774-88ab-b3a6803ec58a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122208} {:answer/id #uuid "34e01c13-4d21-58b8-93f4-500a27533e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122209} {:answer/id #uuid "40c10255-3148-5fd3-a7c7-cbc0ea280617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122210} {:answer/id #uuid "6335f442-a68e-52bc-a082-7c57f56ec474" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e01c13-4d21-58b8-93f4-500a27533e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122209} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7afe34b-b970-5a8d-b5e1-46fd5c6db5df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "83167862-effb-539c-8ffb-5705b88d44f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-36019" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(1,1,1)$ for $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{yz}{x-2z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{yz}{x-2z}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{yz}{(x-2z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\frac{yz}{(x-2z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{z}{(x-2z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-\\frac{z}{(x-2z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1\\cdot (x-2z)^{2}-z\\cdot 2(x-2z)\\cdot (-2)}{(x-2z)^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x-2z)^{2}+4z(x-2z)}{(x-2z)^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x-2z+4z}{(x-2z)^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x+2z}{(x-2z)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(1,1,1) & =-\\frac{1+2\\cdot 1}{(1-2\\cdot 1)^{3}}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc26be90-4e45-51be-ab25-c12b025adcc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321730} {:answer/id #uuid "6af0533d-0474-517b-812d-df525a2684d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321731} {:answer/id #uuid "c5169263-9a5a-55ab-968f-9d22f4170200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321732} {:answer/id #uuid "68aaa6f7-43ba-5322-93aa-ec15065bd52e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321733} {:answer/id #uuid "d054d252-4a25-5c57-8664-65ba70a10267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})+8{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5169263-9a5a-55ab-968f-9d22f4170200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321732} :answer-field/id #uuid "af623079-4435-58c9-ae98-24cc6204c8c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9d636c4-33c5-563b-950f-b4f6d1995bff" :question/math-academy-id "q-65058" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})+2x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c0759e4-732e-53c1-a2a8-4ff5cf6a4a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4xy(1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321737} {:answer/id #uuid "e57b20a3-38f2-56cd-a7be-6dfa986ef801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321738} {:answer/id #uuid "dbab8e1a-1f6a-5ece-8472-c2a77c74fcd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(x+y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321739} {:answer/id #uuid "fd455f85-c943-5ad3-b039-c0e427e03e21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy(1-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321740} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf5f9a8-2f5a-537e-963f-fd71969db3b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y(1-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c0759e4-732e-53c1-a2a8-4ff5cf6a4a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4xy(1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321737} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ea3789-8a92-5b85-ba54-7f672e85ff39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0d3acae-d693-52ff-bd3c-27f29f2d4449" :question/math-academy-id "q-65060" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2x\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2x[2y\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}+{y}^{2}\\cdot ({e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\cdot 2y{x}^{2})] \\\\  & =4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}+4{x}^{3}{y}^{3}{e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =4xy(1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a062bc7-1894-5292-9679-b8f8c2b076db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(1+xy){e}^{xy}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321744} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe95d8d-64e7-5e26-8497-4ba50d04a5a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2-xy){e}^{xy}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321745} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb74cbd-5f37-556f-b5a7-7d97e60fd7b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+xy){e}^{xy}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321746} {:answer/id #uuid "13fa376c-22fa-5bbb-b6ea-2d61be4675f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(2+xy){e}^{xy}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321747} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d65a62-afa0-5619-8421-b4ea789a417f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2-xy){e}^{xy}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13fa376c-22fa-5bbb-b6ea-2d61be4675f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(2+xy){e}^{xy}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321747} :answer-field/id #uuid "29c9042e-e21e-5fb9-812e-4399723e1296" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "496a6dc2-a2be-5cc0-b846-7ba6991e3da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-65068" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}_{xxy}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =y{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =y(y{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{xxy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xx}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot {e}^{xy}+{y}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot x \\\\  & =y(2+xy){e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7eb1695-cfb1-51d5-9b77-e9e9b7ecaebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321751} {:answer/id #uuid "75572fda-0dd9-5031-a2ea-eb17ac3dd1ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4+y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321752} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe517db-b499-5ef7-9194-f08d147ac28a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321753} {:answer/id #uuid "9b008f21-7439-5aee-ac6e-59588a0a877f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321754} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5d3bfd-9923-5575-a61d-6c027a071ca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b008f21-7439-5aee-ac6e-59588a0a877f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321754} :answer-field/id #uuid "0baa3a37-991b-59f6-9209-b96a40755564" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e606e43e-b267-5b19-ab3d-7c9894aaf615" :question/math-academy-id "q-65071" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}_{yxx}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{yxx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{yx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot x-4y\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "547716d8-2300-5856-b406-8d31be6dbe5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y{x}^{2}{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321758} {:answer/id #uuid "607bfe98-13f6-59df-b969-3bca3f7f9d84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(1+2{y}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321759} {:answer/id #uuid "bd918458-ed90-53fa-bdbb-e76b5e749f65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y(1+{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321760} {:answer/id #uuid "b061df2b-118a-5d97-8c0e-ee73b1b4a821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321761} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef14c94-9e3e-5707-9f2a-5b55e365baa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y(1+2{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ef14c94-9e3e-5707-9f2a-5b55e365baa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y(1+2{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321762} :answer-field/id #uuid "154c21bc-fc1a-5414-9e3b-7ecea8257c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67d1b100-b706-537a-83f8-4abae40799eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-80396" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot ({e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}+2{x}^{2}{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y(1+2{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e885de0a-db0c-5a22-a670-4ebecb2360c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321765} {:answer/id #uuid "023b1a1a-ac2b-5f06-a506-ae2819c2add7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321766} {:answer/id #uuid "b0eebbc0-c424-5a28-b715-b73c6cbc7127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321767} {:answer/id #uuid "ac51f9f7-b74c-5fc6-a87e-c63c035449cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321768} {:answer/id #uuid "3767127a-29b0-522d-83b6-f559b618e88d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0eebbc0-c424-5a28-b715-b73c6cbc7127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321767} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a9694dc-d08c-5951-8037-cc6b95b10b98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e44348dd-af5f-5871-b215-119a4f001a40" :question/math-academy-id "q-80456" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+y}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+y}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+y}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+y}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}})\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5976a7d-c044-585f-b196-5d49790837b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321772} {:answer/id #uuid "ee01282a-e242-5b3f-9d68-e369ab91691b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321773} {:answer/id #uuid "595777da-9b6e-5590-a4e4-4e2e29b2a1b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321774} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b8d175-a9dd-58bb-8d2f-95e24742f3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321775} {:answer/id #uuid "adc84c5b-85af-5cff-a902-8749759fcbaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b8d175-a9dd-58bb-8d2f-95e24742f3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321775} :answer-field/id #uuid "e157cfed-9487-5ec6-bb5b-1b0b15476ba4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "deab84e9-a867-5b1d-9a68-3b0761520810" :question/math-academy-id "q-80468" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot (-2y)) \\\\  & =2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =-y(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot 2x) \\\\  & =2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})+2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
